{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Use Spring Framework 6.0 with Java 17+ as baseline",
    "Kafka as the message bus for partition pre-allocation (U3, U4)",
    "Reactor 3.x for reactive stream processing in U6",
    "Microbatching implemented via configurable batch intervals in source modules (U7)",
    "Spark integration via Spring XD's module SPI, using Spark Structured Streaming (U5)",
    "Offset management in Kafka source using Kafka consumer API with manual offset commit (U2)",
    "Partition pre-allocation at deployment time using a centralized partition assigner (U3, U4)",
    "Performance testing on Rackspace using dedicated clusters for Kafka and XD containers"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The team has expertise in Spring, Kafka, Reactor, and Spark",
    "Existing Spring XD codebase is available and modular for adding new modules",
    "Kafka version 2.5+ is used, supporting exactly-once semantics and transactional producers",
    "The wiki documentation (U1) is for internal/confluence wiki, not external",
    "The performance testing infrastructure (U8) is limited to setting up the environment and initial scripts; ongoing testing is out of scope",
    "The reactor-stream processor module (U6) will support a DSL for time-window operations and expressions",
    "Microbatching (U7) will be implemented initially for HTTP source, with extensibility to other sources",
    "Spark POC (U5) will focus on streaming integration, not batch",
    "All development follows test-driven development with unit and integration tests",
    "Deployment model: Spring XD uses a container-based deployment (like YARN, Kubernetes, or standalone). We assume a container orchestration that supports partition assignment."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
